                            {
                                "target_word": "hexadecachoron",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9ca83ca1-a746-362f-9fc2-1b03c1e938d4",
                                        "entry_id": "8c478076-babc-36ad-bcde-78b18807e082",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A four-dimensional object analogous to an octahedron, constructed out of sixteen tetrahedra."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "54e559b2-4d0f-41fe-8696-5a02d7fdfa3c",
                                                "sense_id": "9ca83ca1-a746-362f-9fc2-1b03c1e938d4",
                                                "text": "In a world with four spatial dimensions, for example, we can construct only six regular solids, viz pentatope, tesseract, hexadecachoron, icositetrachoron, hecatonicosachoron and hexacosichoron."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d2db8ed4-7326-4cfe-b3b6-b069b1dfd10f",
                                                "sense_id": "9ca83ca1-a746-362f-9fc2-1b03c1e938d4",
                                                "text": "We have chosen the surfaces of a pentatope (5-cell) as well as a hexadecachoron (16-cell), which are simple standard triangulations of a 3-sphere, shown in figure (7), as our underlying lattices."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ddb8853c-3334-4482-9414-f57ce647c5ec",
                                                "sense_id": "9ca83ca1-a746-362f-9fc2-1b03c1e938d4",
                                                "text": "In four dimensions, surprisingly, there are three space-filling convex regular polychora: the tesseract (the hypercube in ℝ⁴), the hexadecachoron, and the icositetrachoron."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
